  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1209 PM CST Tue Nov 17 2026\n\nThe area remains generally rain free through the end of the week. A \nweak cold front is forecast to move into S Central TX this weekend, \nwith consensus being on Sunday. Models differ on how far south \nthe frontal boundary will go, but generally expecting it to stall \nacross the area. The boundary will provide low level moisture \nconvergence, combined with weak upper support, to bring rain \nchances back into the forecast beginning Saturday night and Sunday\nand continuing into early next week. Location of the highest rain\nchances and amounts is still too soon to forecast due to the \nuncertainty as to where the boundary stalls.",
